{# goal: Apply HT-1 to update the distilled conclusion only on contradiction, new category, recommendation flip or meaningful refinement; reconfirmation keeps the prior text. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    cycle_events: array
    prior_conclusion: string|null
  output:
    gate_trigger: string
    gate_reason: string
    updated_conclusion: string
---

Classify one hypothesis-testing cycle against its prior distilled conclusion.

- cycle_events: {{ cycle_events | tojson }}
- prior_conclusion: {{ prior_conclusion if prior_conclusion else "(none)" }}

Choose exactly one trigger: `contradiction`, `new_category`, `flip`, `refinement`, `reconfirmation`. If no prior conclusion exists, use `new_category`. A refinement names the dimension narrowed, broadened or qualified.

On the first four triggers, produce one concise updated paragraph. On `reconfirmation`, return the prior conclusion verbatim. Do not smuggle new claims through reconfirmation.

Return JSON only with exactly `gate_trigger`, `gate_reason`, `updated_conclusion`.
